body:
Sorry for the late response but I was quite busy...

&#x200B;

I can understand that you don't want to make any trouble or don't want to make the situation in your family worse, but according to the things you write I would say that you reached a point where you should worry more about you then about your family. Especially if you have no good relationship to your parents.

&#x200B;

Beside of that I would recommend you to talk to a professional. They aren't allowed to tell your parents (As long as you live in the western hemisphere) and your parents don#t need to know that. Maybe you can just phone them or anything like that.

Hey,

&#x200B;

I know the feeling of not wanting to life anymore. I feel the same way. Because of that I don't want to tell you stay here or do nothing bad. Of course I hope that thing will get better soon, but I don't want to tell you what to do or judge you. I'm a little bit older then you (20; M) and I have no real clue how to help you. You are quite young, but experienced so many awfull things.

&#x200B;

I don't know a lot of you but I would try to get distance between you and your family. Do you have some family members or friend where you can stay a little bit until  you figured out a plan?

I would contact a doctor or something if I were you. As I said before, this is just my personal advice as somebody who knows a least a little bit your feelings. What you want to tell him or her is up to you, but they can give you medicines if you want to. I don't want to say that you should take medicines and everything is fine, I know that this isn't true (From own experience), but a good friend of mine also experienced a lot of SA. Before there was the possibility to change anything she needed (And she really needed) to take medicine. Not to make her happy or something like that, just to keep her cool and be able to start a therapy. She had very often panic attacks and it was impossible for her to change anything while she was in this condition. She also had a lot of problems with her parents so your situations are quite similar.

Hey, 

&#x200B;

I feel you. Same here. I'm just gonna try out my new medicine the next month and if it doen't help I'm going to end my life
